# Subagent Council Loop (mandatory — NOT Gauntlet)

**NOT:** Gauntlet loop · gauntlet-critic · BAR · scores · “make gate green.”

**Full doc:** `docs/qa/SUBAGENT_COUNCIL_LOOP.md` (charters, **owner-approved exceptions registry**, proposal minimum, verify routing)

Do **not** apply gameplay/planning fixes until council passes.

**Permanent report mandate (owner 2026-09-01):** Every fix turn must show **what fixed** + **per-critic PASS proof in chat before apply**. See `.cursor/rules/council-report-mandatory.mdc` and `docs/qa/COUNCIL_REPORT_MANDATE.md`. Headline QA delta without proof table = **invalid report**. “6/6 PASS” without critic rows = **forgery**.

---

## Loop

```
PROPOSE (no code) → COUNCIL (parallel) → all PASS → APPLY → VERIFY (automated QA)
```

Any FAIL → revise proposal → new council. Do not apply partial fixes from critics.

**Post-apply amendments:** Any code change after council PASS → **amendment council** on full delta before layer DONE. Log in `docs/qa/COUNCIL_AUDIT_LOG.md`.

**Remediation:** If council was skipped → remediation council on shipped scope; log verdict before layer stays DONE.

**Proposal must name behavioral tests** for bible rules touched. Structural grep alone = instant FAIL.

---

## Council size (efficient)

| Scope | Critics |
|-------|---------|
| **Default** planning / paint / commit / hover | **5** parallel (charters 1–5 in doc) |
| + QA FAIL / test edits | **+ Critic 6** |
| + class factory / skills | **+ Critic 7** |

Launch all in **one message**. Verdict: **all PASS** (5/5, 6/6, or 7/7).

Subagent: **generalPurpose** with charter from doc. **Not** `gauntlet-critic`.

---

## Critics (summary — detail in doc)

1. **Bible paint & tiles** — locked vs bundle (EX-LOCKED-FIELD), path vs flood, EX-BIBLE-UI, behavioral tests in proposal  
2. **Settle / bundle / commit** — Director + Simulator owners, ratify, no post-process redo, EX-FROZEN-REPLAY, EX-PERF-SCHED at flush  
3. **Stand & range origins** — phase-entry, two-range model, EX-POSTMOVE-SLOT  
4. **Global systems & anti-heuristic** — 6-row audit, exception IDs cited correctly, no silent bypass  
5. **Perf & scheduling** — EX-PERF-SCHED guardian; cheap-walk slot parity; locked paint stable under throttle  
6. *(optional)* **QA-fix discipline** — `qa-fix-no-heuristics`  
7. *(optional)* **Class / skill scope** — `skill-global-rules`, EX-CLASS-QA-SCOPE  

Each returns **PASS/FAIL + rule or exception ID cites only**. No scores.

---

## Owner-approved exceptions (few — critics enforce)

See full registry in `docs/qa/SUBAGENT_COUNCIL_LOOP.md`. Key IDs:

| ID | One line |
|----|----------|
| **EX-PERF-SCHED** | Throttle + cheap walk inside canonical owner; flush before ratify |
| **EX-LOCKED-FIELD** | Locked blue/red outside hover bundle — plan revision keyed |
| **EX-BIBLE-UI** | Teleport hop + push/pull separate UI |
| **EX-FROZEN-REPLAY** | Sealed path display-only — no re-sim |
| **EX-POSTMOVE-SLOT** | Documented POSTMOVE/modular cursor only |
| **EX-SIM-REJECT** | Fail loud — no commit fixup of preview |
| **EX-INTENT-DIVERGE** | Only with owner ⚠ yes |
| **EX-CLASS-QA-SCOPE** | Drag/undo not on every skill row |

Do **not** FAIL correct exception use. **Do** FAIL misuse, deletion, or relabeling as “heuristic cleanup.”

---

## After council

- **All PASS:** **publish council proof table in chat (before apply)** → apply → QA per `qa-after-gameplay-changes.mdc` → changelog `### Council proof (pre-apply)` + `### What fixed` + audit log entry with **same table** + commit hash  
- **Swap-only:** `run_swap_planning_acceptance.ps1` during iteration  
- **Any FAIL:** new proposal → new council  

**Forbidden:** `Council: N/N PASS` without per-critic rows · council logged post-commit · QA count as opening headline without proof block.

Structural gates after apply are **not** council substitutes.
